A||||14||FIEROCIOUS||So, I called IRM today.....||||5||
Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||02-02-2001||05:31 AM||||So, I called IRM today, A guy answered "IRM can I help you?" I said "Yeah, I need a catalog." Then he replied "Um, uh, can you call back later and ask for Barbara?" I said "Sure." I didn't have a chance to call back today. I was planning on ordering some integrated rocker panels, and was wondering how IRM is to do business with? How fast did you recieve your parts were you happy ect. I know some of you know the people at IRM well so let me know. I did think a simple catalog request wouldn't require a second call. <P>Thanks all! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||02-02-2001||10:03 AM||||The guy that answered the phone was probably Jim. He had a stroke a couple of years ago. I think that Barbara has taken it upon herself to handle most of the Fiero related stuff. From what I've heard, they are very committed to keeping IRM "alive and well", and serving the Fiero community, but they have to take things slow, due to Jim's health problems. Their major line of work is, or used to be, electronics. The Fiero thing was secondary, although they seem to be very passionate about it. (I think several folks have approached them, trying to buy the Fiero business. NOT gonna happen.) I have never heard anything bad about IRM. <BR>If they have stuff in stock, they can usually ship within a couple of days. <BR>Just gotta be patient.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Just my $.02.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 02-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||02-02-2001||10:31 AM||||i got the integrated rocker panels and an indy scoop from them and both took a pretty long time. i think those are both items they make to order. same with the catalog though. took a few months to get it a few years back. once i got them i was happy with them (want a couple more indy scoops and maybe another pair of rocker panels), but i know now to expect to wait.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||02-02-2001||10:51 AM||||I and others around me have ordered from IRM. The parts received were made well but not exactly "ready to paint" They still required some finishing work. As for time, Yes it does take a while to get the parts if they are not in stock. I was told when I ordered my Indy scoop that it would be 6-8 weeks and it took about that long. I think most of the custom fiberglass stuff is "made to order" The larger parts take even longer.<BR>Example: front air dam for an 84 took 3 months. Everyone was told up front that the parts not in stock took a lot of time. Out of all who have ordered parts, the biggest thing was the finishing work required. This isn't a bad thing, just something people mentioned the most. If you know up front it requires more finishing work then it's not a shock when you receive the parts. Otherwise I and the others seem happy with the items. (I really like my Indy scoop!)  If I ever find an 84 with 4-spd locally and inexpensive I would order the IMSA body kit for the car from them.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||02-02-2001||12:06 PM||||How's the finish on the integrated rocker panels?  What's the price, too?  I really want a set of these..||||reg||
Z||000005||Oreif||02-02-2001||12:15 PM||||The panels require some finishing sanding and a little filing for fit. Cost is $550.00 for the set.<BR>This link goes to an IRM catalog that was scanned in.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||02-02-2001||12:33 PM||||What was their price on the Indy Scoop?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||02-02-2001||02:20 PM||||In my previous post is the link to the catalog with prices. Indy Scoop $200.00<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Voytek||02-02-2001||02:55 PM||||I have ordered a couple 5" wing stands from IRM.  It took them about 4 weeks and 5 phonecalls from me to get them.  Twice I was told that the parts have shipped when they had not.  The stands did not match the lid's profile very well and the brackets inside them were a bit too large (unfortunately modifying the brackets is a b**ch!!).  My trunk has been leaking ever since.||||reg||1
Z||000009||pred1tor83||02-02-2001||07:52 PM||||maybe they should get a web site!!||||reg||3
Z||000010||FIEROCIOUS||02-02-2001||11:36 PM||||Thanks, for the replies, I do hate to nag companies for my order! But if they tell me up front I guess I could handle that? I once ordered an intake and after a month I called the company back and "Oh yeah, we wondered who ordered that?" "It's all boxed and ready to ship we just forgot who to?" Told them don't bother! If you guys say they are good and won't "forget my order" I will definately give them a call!<P>Thanks guys and gals!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Standard||02-03-2001||04:52 AM||||'nother quick question..<P>The integrated rocker panels completely replace the ground f/x and body panels, right?  It's hard to tell from the pics...||||reg||
Z||000012||danny boy||02-03-2001||01:24 PM|||| It took me six calls and I never did get a catalog... there stuff is really nice if you can get it from them, though. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Philphine||02-03-2001||05:22 PM||||the rocker panels replace the section behind the door,rocker panels, and the ground effects. i don't know if you have to take the section on the door off,since i have a coupe. also the secton behind the front wheel stays but you trim a few inches off of it.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||02-04-2001||02:56 AM||||From what I've seen, you can either leave the door fx on or take them off.  Personally, I think it looks <B>much</B> better if the door fx come off.||||reg||1
